# Build output. `build/` has no leading slash, so it matches the root project's and every
# module's, at any depth — including composeApp/build/outputs/mapping/, R8's symbol map, which
# is a build artifact even though RELEASING.md says to keep a copy of it.
build/
out/
captures/

# Gradle's and Kotlin's own caches. Machine-local and regenerated on demand.
.gradle/
.kotlin/
*.hprof

# Where the Android SDK lives on this machine. Every checkout has a different answer, which is
# why the build reads it from here rather than from a committed file.
local.properties

# The Firebase config. Per-deployment, names the Play package, and is the difference between a
# build that can receive a push and one that cannot — so it is a credential, not configuration.
# CI writes it from GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON_BASE64; a clone without it still builds and runs.
composeApp/google-services.json
# And wherever a copy gets dropped on the way in. The pattern rather than the one path that exists
# today: these arrive from a browser download with names like `google-services (4).json`, and the
# copy nobody meant to keep is the one that gets committed.
google-services*.json
# The same thing for iOS (iosApp/iosApp/GoogleService-Info.plist), under any download name. CI
# writes it from GOOGLE_SERVICE_INFO_PLIST_BASE64; without it the app builds with push inert.
GoogleService-Info*.plist
# Manual signing for one TestFlight run, written by scripts/ios-ci-signing.py.
iosApp/Configuration/Signing.xcconfig

# Xcode's per-user state and derived data, and the Kotlin/Native caches.
iosApp/build/
xcuserdata/
.kotlin/
*.p8
*.mobileprovision

# Anything that could sign or publish a release. The directory rather than a pattern per file,
# so a secret added later is ignored before anyone has to remember to add it — and the keystore
# patterns as well, for a key someone drops outside it.
.secrets/
composeApp/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# IDEs and editors. The Gradle build is the source of truth; nobody should need another
# checkout's project files to open this one.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# The web target's toolchain. `kotlin-js-store/yarn.lock` is deliberately *not* here: it pins
# the Wasm build's npm dependencies and belongs in the repository.
node_modules/

# Scratch output from tools that run against the app — MCP browser sessions, the Python in
# play/ — none of which is part of the app.
.playwright-mcp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# What the console Unitool writes when it is tried out from the repository root: the README's
# `unitool qr … -o code.png` lands here, and `--split` adds export-1.png, export-2.png, … Only the
# root, so pictures that belong to the app (docs/, play/, the modules' resources) stay tracked.
/*.png
/*.svg

# A symlink to an unrelated checkout on one machine, used as reference material. It would be
# committed as a dangling symlink for everyone else.
/example-app

# A symlink to the Node/TypeScript framework this one is modelled on, kept as a reference while
# working. It is somebody else's repository, not a dependency of this build.
/adminizer

# The library's checkout, when it is next door. settings.gradle.kts picks it up automatically;
# it has its own git.
/superizer

# OS droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local secrets (MCP key of unitool-server, …) — never committed.
.env

# Release credentials kept next to the notes (App Store Connect key, Firebase admin keys, provisioning
# profile). Never in git.
.ai-notes/keys/
# A link to the server checkout (/prj/layers-fw/unitool-server), its own repository.
/unitool-server
